+# Todo Due Date Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add optional due dates, a UTC-based overdue status, and overdue-only filtering to the todo API and list for ticket 1.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep the singleton TodoStore as the shared source for API and Blazor. Store calendar dates, inject TimeProvider, and produce fresh response snapshots with a derived overdue status. Distinguish an omitted PATCH date from explicit null through a presence-tracking property on TodoPatch.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor interactive server, System.Text.Json, xUnit, WebApplicationFactory, Playwright MCP. No new NuGet packages.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-23-todo-due-date-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Overdue means `!Done && DueDate < today (UTC)`; missing dates and today are never overdue.
+- Exact UI text: `überfällig` and `nur überfällige`.
+- Dates use `YYYY-MM-DD`; API responses include `dueDate` and `isOverdue`.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` filters; omitted or false returns everything in existing order.
+- PATCH omission preserves the date; explicit null removes it.
+- Todo editing happens only through the API; the page calls the store directly.
+- No new NuGet packages, persistence, sorting, or automatic midnight page refresh.
+- Test-dependent new elements carry `data-testid` attributes.
+- Agent performs Playwright end-to-end verification; screenshots stay outside the repository.
+- Finish with a draft PR against main on branch `1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos`; never merge or close the ticket.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- UTC midnight must refresh the status of existing records without a write (Task 1).
+- A title-only or done-only PATCH must preserve the due date (Tasks 1 and 2).
+- Invalid dates, non-date JSON values, and invalid filter values must return JSON errors without mutation (Task 2).
+- Completing and reopening an old dated todo must update its filter membership (Tasks 1 and 2).
+- Empty filter results and toggling back must leave all original items available (Task 3 and Playwright).
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store dates, current status, and filtering
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/TodoStore.cs`, `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoStoreTests.cs`; create `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TestTimeProvider.cs`.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- `Todo(int Id, string Title, bool Done, DateOnly? DueDate = null, bool IsOverdue = false)` is the immutable result snapshot.
+- `NewTodo(string? Title, DateOnly? DueDate = null)` preserves old callers.
+- `TodoPatch(string? Title, bool? Done)` gains an init-settable `DateOnly? DueDate` and JSON-ignored `bool HasDueDate`; setting DueDate, including null, sets presence.
+- `TodoStore(TimeProvider? timeProvider = null)` defaults to TimeProvider.System for existing direct callers.
+- `IReadOnlyList<Todo> List(bool overdue = false)`; existing Get, Add, Update and Remove signatures remain.
+- Store private immutable state without IsOverdue; convert to snapshots using a single captured UTC date per operation. API and UI both consume these snapshots.
+- TestTimeProvider derives from TimeProvider; exposes `SetUtcNow(DateTimeOffset)` and overrides GetUtcNow.
+
+- [x] **Step 1: Write failing store tests and the test clock.** Cover missing/explicit-null dates, yesterday/today/tomorrow, done todos, setting/replacing/clearing dates, omitted dates on title/done updates, stable ordering, empty filters, completion/reopening, and an existing record across UTC midnight. Representative assertions:
+
+```csharp
+Assert.Null(store.Add(new NewTodo("No date")).DueDate);
+Assert.True(store.Add(new NewTodo("Late", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 22))).IsOverdue);
+Assert.False(store.Add(new NewTodo("Today", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 23))).IsOverdue);
+Assert.Equal(original.DueDate, store.Update(original.Id, new TodoPatch("Renamed", null))!.DueDate);
+Assert.Null(store.Update(original.Id, new TodoPatch(null, null) { DueDate = null })!.DueDate);
+Assert.All(store.List(true), todo => Assert.True(todo.IsOverdue));
+```
+
+- [x] **Step 2: Run `dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~TodoStoreTests`.** Confirm failures are missing due-date interfaces/behavior.
+- [x] **Step 3: Implement the interfaces above in TodoStore.cs.** Use DateOnly.FromDateTime(timeProvider.GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime), retain locking and validation, and project snapshots while holding the lock. Never mutate dates during reads.
+- [x] **Step 4: Run the store tests.** All pass, including the original tests and the UTC transition without a write.
+- [x] **Step 5: Commit** store and tests as `feat: add due dates and overdue filtering to todo store`.
+
+### Task 2: Expose dates and filtering through the API
+
